	"title"		"More Props BETA"
	"description"		"[h1]🌳 MORE PROPS BETA (256K EDITION) 🌳[/h1]
[b]The 262,144 User Props Limit Breaker & Virtual Active Window Engine for Cities: Skylines[/b]
[i]Engineered with high-performance 32-bit spatial partitioning and seamless 16-bit tool hot-swapping by NgocDuy[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]🌟 OVERVIEW: QUADRUPLED PROP CAPACITY[/h1]
Have you ever hit the infamous [b]Prop Limit (65,536 props)[/b] when detailing sprawling downtowns, lush forested parks, realistic highways, or complex railway networks?
In vanilla Cities: Skylines, [b]PropManager.MAX_PROPS_LIMIT is hard-coded at 65,536[/b] (16-bit ushort). Once reached, the game permanently refuses to place any more props, and cloning props with Move It fails completely.

[b]More Props BETA[/b] safely expands the user prop ceiling to [b]262,144 props (256K)[/b] — a massive [b]400% capacity boost[/b]!

[list]
[*] [b]Vanilla Limit:[/b] 65,536 Props
[*] [b]More Props BETA Limit:[/b] [b]262,144 Props (256K / 2^18)[/b]
[*] [b]Compatibility:[/b] [b]100% Native support for Move It, Prop Line Tool, Find It! 2, Forest Brush, Prop Control, Prop & Tree Anarchy[/b]
[*] [b]Save Safety:[/b] Dual-stream serialization with Asset String Table (immune to asset re-index)
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]⚡ ARCHITECTURAL BREAKTHROUGH: VIRTUAL 16-BIT ACTIVE WINDOW[/h1]
Unlike naive implementations that break 16-bit mod compatibility, More Props BETA uses a state-of-the-art [b]Virtual 16-bit Active Window (Hot-Swapping Pool)[/b]:

[list]
[*] [b]The Problem:[/b] Core tool mods like [b]Move It (MoveableProp)[/b] and Prop Tool communicate strictly via 16-bit [i]InstanceID.Prop (ushort)[/i]. Forcing 32-bit IDs causes catastrophic exceptions in Move It.
[*] [b]The Solution:[/b] The vanilla 65K array is preserved as an active dynamic interaction buffer. The full 262,144 props live in our extended 32-bit storage grid.
[*] [b]Zero-Latency Hot-Swapping:[/b] When your cursor moves over any prop or when you drag a Move It marquee selection box, the props in those grid cells are instantly mounted into free ushort slots.
[*] [b]Bi-directional Instant Sync:[/b] Any translation, rotation, elevation, cloning, or deletion done in Move It is instantly synced back to the extended 256K database in real time!
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]🎮 FEATURES AT A GLANCE[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Full Move It 100% Compatibility:[/b] Drag, rotate, clone, elevate, align, and copy-paste any prop in the 262,144 universe seamlessly!
[*] [b]Optimized Frustum & LOD Batching Renderer:[/b] Unmounted props are rendered with native camera frustum culling and hardware-accelerated LOD instancing, ensuring smooth 60 FPS even with 200,000+ props.
[*] [b]String Table Save Protection:[/b] Extended props are serialized with their full asset prefab names. If you unsubscribe from a Workshop prop or your asset list changes order, your other props will never disappear or get swapped!
[*] [b]In-Game HUD Monitor:[/b] Press [b]Alt + P[/b] anytime in-game to view real-time Active Buffer usage and Total 256K Props placed.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]🔧 COMPATIBILITY & REQUIREMENTS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Harmony 2.x:[/b] Self-contained via CitiesHarmony.
[*] [b]Incompatible Mods:[/b] Extended Managers Library (EML) and Quayhuan's Prop Anarchy (which hard-requires EML). (Do not run simultaneously).
[*] [b]Fully Compatible:[/b] Move It, Prop Line Tool (PLT), Find It! 2, Prop Control (by algernon), classic Prop & Tree Anarchy (by BloodyPenguin), Forest Brush, Network Multitool, Node Controller, TM:PE.
[/list]

[b]Developed with precision by NgocDuy[/b]"
	"changenote"		"v1.0.6-BETA: CRASH SHIELD & RENDERING HARDENING:
1. Eliminated TerrainModify IndexOutOfRangeException: Rewrote UnmountProp to directly and safely recycle active vanilla slots via RemoveFromVanillaGrid and ReleaseItem under synchronized lock, bypassing vanilla PropManager.ReleaseProp. This prevents unnecessary TerrainModify/UpdateArea calculations on unmounted props, completely eliminating IndexOutOfRangeException crashes in Building/NetSegment.TerrainUpdated and preventing vanilla slot leaks.
2. Armored LOD Batch Renderer Against ArgumentNullException: ExtendedPropRenderer now automatically detects and provides appropriate HeightMapping and WaterMapping textures via TerrainManager when rendering unmounted props (quays, decals, rocks, water vegetation). This eliminates the MaterialPropertyBlock.SetTexture null argument exception during batch LOD flushes.
3. Added Native View Frustum Culling: Integrated CameraInfo.Intersect culling into ExtendedPropRenderer, skipping off-screen unmounted props before transform/matrix calculations for maximum framerate stability.
4. Resilient LOD Error Absorption: Wrapped batch LOD flushes in try-catch blocks with automatic lodCount reset, isolating broken Workshop assets and preventing render frame disruptions."
}

